// Part of the Plew compiler module (root: _.pw). The code-emission backend: walk
// the analyzed arena `runFrontend()` produces and build a real LLVM module in
// process through libLLVM-C (spec/15 FFI). The compiler links libLLVM (only this
// part references it) and emits the module as text via LLVMPrintModuleToString ->
// stdout, linked against a small C runtime emitted by `plewc --runtime`
// (PlewString / plew_* are the ABI the generated IR targets).
//
// COVERAGE: the entry module's `main` + plain free functions (params, returns,
// recursion, default args, lexical scope/shadowing); width-accurate integers
// (i8/i16/i32/i64 with sext/zext/trunc coercion at typed sinks — literal width
// from the suffix or the checker's exprIntCtx; add/sub/mul/div/rem/neg are
// overflow- and div-by-zero-checked via the `plew_<w><Op>` runtime floor, loud
// (wrapping is opt-in via wrapping* methods); the
// full operator set (arithmetic / bitwise / shift / unary / comparison; >> is
// arithmetic, a logical-shift-on-unsigned TODO); Bool; String (value `{ptr,i64}`,
// literals, ==/!=); `if`/`while`; and the intrinsics exit / write / eprint /
// print / panic (print dispatches by the arg's type-kind to a runtime formatter).
// A per-local type-kind tag (int/String/Bool/uint) drives String-vs-int and
// signed-vs-unsigned decisions without c.locals (which the backend doesn't
// populate). NOT yet: structs/enums, arrays, generics, methods, closures, async,
// ARC, multi-module user code (only module 0 is emitted). Anything unsupported is
// rejected loudly (no silent miscompile — acceptance soundness).

//
// The emitter is split across `Llvm/` for readability (one concern per file);
// all parts share the module scope, so the split is purely organizational.

part ./Llvm/Bindings
part ./Llvm/State
part ./Llvm/Types
part ./Llvm/Enums
part ./Llvm/GenericStruct
part ./Llvm/GenericQuery
part ./Llvm/GenericAny
part ./Llvm/Locals
part ./Llvm/StringOps
part ./Llvm/Arith
part ./Llvm/Expr
part ./Llvm/ExprControl
part ./Llvm/Arrays
part ./Llvm/ArrayOps
part ./Llvm/Iter
part ./Llvm/CallBasic
part ./Llvm/CallExt
part ./Llvm/CallMethod
part ./Llvm/CallGeneric
part ./Llvm/AssocFns
part ./Llvm/ProvidedFns
part ./Llvm/GenMethods
part ./Llvm/Closures
part ./Llvm/Thunks
part ./Llvm/Any
part ./Llvm/Stmt
part ./Llvm/StmtMatch
part ./Llvm/StmtFor
part ./Llvm/StmtDeinit
part ./Llvm/Entry
part ./Llvm/Async
part ./Llvm/Runtime
